**ARCHITECT: Claude (Anthropic)  ·  CODE EXECUTOR: Gemini**

*This document is the single source of truth for the DPC Hub build. The code executor (Gemini) must read this document in full before writing any code. Every architectural decision is locked here. If something is underspecified, stop and flag it — do not improvise. If this document conflicts with any other document, this document wins.*

*Governance note: This work is organic. There are no scheduled review dates, governance milestones, or phase gates tied to calendar dates. Progress is measured by build phase completion, not time elapsed.*

**Document 1 — Vision ****&**** Principles**

**1.1  What this system is**

The DPC Hub is the personal operating system for the Digital Pedagogy Coach (DPC) role at Weston College Group. It is a coaching intelligence platform — not an IT system, not a compliance tracker, not a staff monitoring tool. Its purpose is to capture evidence of practice, support structured professional conversations, close the loop between observation and improvement, and produce meaningful reports for different audiences at different levels of detail.

The DPC role operates across 35 curriculum areas with no formal authority. Influence flows through relational capital, coaching conversations, and making it easy for people to lead in their own areas. The Hub serves that model — it does not replace professional judgement, it informs and evidences it.

**1.2  The two systems**

The DPC Hub is two connected but independent deployments:

- DPC Hub (desktop) — the full system. Runs in Edge on a Windows college laptop. All sensitive data lives here. Password protected. One user: Graeme Wright.

- Hub Lite (mobile) — a surface-layer only companion. Non-confidential data only. Available on phone without opening a laptop. Quick Capture for notes and meeting shells. Calendar surface (what/where/who/date/time only). No drill-down. No sensitive data. Syncs to the Hub on next desktop open.

**1.3  Non-negotiable principles**

| **WCAG 2.2 AA** | Every UI component, every output document, every publicly accessible HTML page meets WCAG 2.2 AA minimum. This is a build gate on every phase, not a final polish. Semi-transparent overlays must be pixel-sampled, not token-estimated. |
| --- | --- |
| **Digital supports TLA** | Digital tools support and enhance exceptional teaching, learning and assessment. They do not replace it. The question is always: what is the rationale, and what is the expected impact on learning? |
| **Evidence must be genuine** | Only real, completed activity is recorded or reported. No overclaiming. No fabrication. QIP contributions are framed honestly. |
| **Coaching not monitoring** | Staff profiles hold coaching conversation records and development priorities — not HR, capability, or appraisal data. The system must never be used or described as a monitoring tool. |
| **DPC as quality filter** | All incoming data (Health Check uploads, reflection submissions, Supabase captures) is reviewed by the DPC before entering the permanent record. The DPC's professional judgement is always the final word. |
| **One source of truth** | Every document references the canonical schema (Document 3). No document restates schema fields — it references them. If the schema changes, bump the version and delete the old copy. |
| **Files touched once** | Each file is built in one phase and only extended in a later phase with explicit scope. No file is restructured mid-build. |
| **Stop and flag** | If the executor encounters something underspecified, stop and flag it. Do not improvise. Do not infer. Raise the question. |

**Document 2 — System Architecture**

**2.1  The three-tier data model**

| **Tier 1 — Public content (GitHub repo: dpc-cpd-library)** | WalkThru cards, resource metadata, LinkedIn pathway links, published CPD resources. Not sensitive. Lives in the repo as JSON files. The public CPD Library HTML reads from here. Anyone can access it. Cards added via an admin form that writes to the repo via GitHub API using a personal access token stored in the browser session only — never in any HTML file. |
| --- | --- |
| **Tier 2 — Operational data (OneDrive JSON files)** | Staff profiles, AFI records, coaching notes, referral records, activity logs, reflections, Health Check scores, RAG ratings, calendar/task entries, template library, teach meet plans, coaching question sets. Sensitive. Lives on OneDrive as structured JSON files. The Hub loads them via File System Access API (weekly permission grant, Monday morning prompt). Auto-saves every 60 seconds during session. No Supabase, no external database, no CE+ issues. |
| **Tier 3 — Non-confidential capture (Supabase — Hub Lite only)** | Meeting shells (date, time, person, area, type, free-text note), quick notes, calendar surface entries. No coaching observations, no AFI details, no staff performance data. One-directional: Hub Lite writes to Supabase, Hub desktop reads pending captures on open and prompts DPC to review before committing to Tier 2. |

**2.2  The two GitHub repositories**

| **gwc25/dpc-hub** | The desktop Hub application. All operational modules. Reads from OneDrive JSON (Tier 2). Reads public resource data from dpc-cpd-library repo on load (cached). Password protected. Single user. |
| --- | --- |
| **gwc25/dpc-cpd-library** | The public CPD Library. WalkThru cards, resources, LinkedIn pathways, booking link. Publicly accessible. No login. The Hub also reads from this repo's JSON files. Admin form writes new cards here via GitHub API. |

**2.3  OneDrive file structure**

All Tier 2 files live in one OneDrive folder: DPC Hub / Data. The manifest file is the only file the DPC manually selects on Hub open — all others are loaded automatically.

| **dpc-manifest.json** | MASTER INDEX. Lightweight. Contains paths to all other data files, last-sync timestamps, Hub version, and user preferences. This is the only file the DPC selects on open. Everything else is referenced from here. |
| --- | --- |
| **data-areas.json** | 35 area records. RAG ratings per dimension, Health Check scores, activity logs, open actions, AFI references, Digital Lead identity, HoA identity, area code. |
| **data-staff.json** | Staff profiles. Dynamically created. Name, area(s), role, entry pathway, ETF stage, three development priorities, full touch history, reflection references. |
| **data-afi.json** | All AFI records with full lifecycle. parentObservation, stage, description, digital opportunity, status, closeWindow, evidence chain, linked actions. |
| **data-calendar.json** | Shadow calendar. Meetings (named people, area, type, date/time, notes ref), tasks (title, project link, start, deadline, status, micro-tasks), dedicated work blocks. |
| **data-reflections.json** | All reflection submissions. Tagged to event, area, AFI. Named at individual level, anonymous at area level. immediate / follow-up stage. |
| **data-templates.json** | Teach Meet plans, coaching question sets, meeting agenda templates. Versioned — each edit creates a new version; instances reference the version they used. |
| **data-cpd.json** | DPC personal CPD log. Events, notes, resources, post-impact confidence rating, actions arising. |
| **data-digital-leads.json** | Digital Lead profiles. 1:1 meeting history, resources created, progress picture, support delivered, impact evidence. |
| **data-current-focus.json** | Targeted focus objects. Flexible — area, person, action, or theme. What/Why/How/Who/Impact fields. SEND is first entry September 2026. |

**2.4  File System Access API — weekly permission model**

The Hub uses the File System Access API (supported in Edge and Chrome on Windows) to read and write directly to the OneDrive-synced local folder. No downloads, no uploads, no zip files.

- First use: DPC grants permission to the OneDrive/DPC Hub/Data folder. Permission persists for 7 days.

- Every Monday morning (or first open of the week): Hub detects expired permission and shows a friendly "Good morning — reconnect to your data folder" prompt. DPC clicks once to re-grant. Hub shows a summary of last week's activity as a purposeful start-of-week check-in.

- Auto-save: every 60 seconds during a session, Hub writes changed files only (not all files). A small "Saved ✓" indicator appears briefly.

- If laptop closes without saving: localStorage holds a session snapshot. On next open, Hub detects the snapshot and offers one-click restore.

- Fallback: if File System Access API unavailable (wrong browser, different device): Hub falls back to localStorage only and prompts DPC to reconnect to OneDrive on return to Edge.

**2.5  Supabase schema (Hub Lite only)**

Non-confidential capture only. One table: hub_lite_captures.

| **id** | UUID, auto-generated |
| --- | --- |
| **capture_type** | enum: meeting_shell │ quick_note │ calendar_entry |
| **captured_at** | ISO timestamp |
| **person_name** | Free text. Non-confidential. |
| **area_code** | Three-letter code (BUI, CON etc). Non-confidential. |
| **meeting_type** | Free text or enum. Non-confidential. |
| **note_text** | Free text. Non-confidential. No coaching observations, no AFI details. |
| **date_time** | ISO timestamp of the event being captured. |
| **synced_to_hub** | Boolean. False until DPC reviews and commits on desktop. |

Row-level security: Supabase anon key used for inserts from Hub Lite. Hub desktop reads via service role key stored in dpc-manifest.json (never in any public HTML).

**Document 3 — Canonical Data Schema  [KEYSTONE]**

This is the single source of truth for every data object in the system. All other documents reference this. None restate it. If a field name here conflicts with any other document, this document wins. Version: 1.0 — July 2026.

*EXECUTOR INSTRUCTION: Before writing any code that reads or writes data, re-read this section. Every field name, type, and relationship is locked here. Do not invent fields. Do not rename fields. If a required field is missing from this schema, stop and flag it.*

**3.1  Area record  (data-areas.json → areas[])**

| **areaCode** | String. 3-letter unique identifier. PRIMARY JOIN KEY across all systems. e.g. BUI, CON, HBH. |
| --- | --- |
| **areaName** | String. Full curriculum area name. |
| **hoaName** | String. Head of Area name. |
| **digitalLeadId** | String. References staff.staffId of the Digital Lead for this area. |
| **campus** | String. Campus location. |
| **pyramidLevel** | enum: foundations │ inclusion │ innovation. Current overall assessment. |
| **ragDimensions** | Object. 8 keys — see 3.1a below. |
| **healthChecks** | Array of HealthCheckRecord objects — see 3.3. |
| **activityLog** | Array of ActivityEntry objects — see 3.4. |
| **afiRefs** | Array of AFI IDs (strings). References data-afi.json. |
| **actionPoints** | Array of ActionPoint objects — see 3.5. |
| **staffRefs** | Array of staffId strings. All staff touched in this area. |
| **notes** | String. Free text area notes. |
| **lastUpdated** | ISO timestamp. |

