**3.10  LRA Observation taxonomy (hardcoded — not in JSON)**

The LRA taxonomy is hardcoded in the Hub's JavaScript as a constant (LRA_TAXONOMY). It does not change between sessions and does not need to be in a data file. The 26/27 taxonomy has 7 categories and 30 themes:

| **Category** | **Theme ID — Label** | **Description (summary)** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Planning and Sequencing of Learning | LI — Learning Intentions | Clear, limitless, aligned to curriculum knowledge, skills and behaviours. |
| 1. Planning and Sequencing of Learning | BB — Building Blocks | Step-by-step structure; each task builds on the last. |
| 1. Planning and Sequencing of Learning | SP — Starting Points | Initial assessment and vocational starting points inform pitch and planning. |
| 1. Planning and Sequencing of Learning | LL — Lasting Learning | Designed to help learners recall, repeat and gain deeper knowledge over time. |
| 2. Inclusive TLA & SEND | PL — Personalised Learning | Staff know learners as individuals based on well-informed sources. |
| 2. Inclusive TLA & SEND | AR — Accessible Resources | Materials clear, easy to use, inclusive in layout and language. |
| 2. Inclusive TLA & SEND | ARD — Accessible Resources (Digital) | Digital materials meet accessibility standards; AT coaching embedded. |
| 2. Inclusive TLA & SEND | LL2 — Language & Literacy Skills | Natural opportunities for literacy and language development built in. |
| 2. Inclusive TLA & SEND | NS — Numeracy Skills | Natural opportunities for numeracy development built in. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | LE — Learning Environment | Safe, structured spaces; learners focused, engaged, valued. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | LED — Learning Environment (Digital nav) | Learners navigate digital spaces easily; fewest clicks; personalise independently. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | RL — Readiness to Learn | R.E.A.D.Y framework; settled environment; learning routines. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | PR — Positive Relationships | Trust, motivation and belonging through positive staff-learner relationships. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | BR — Behaviour Regulation | Staff support emotion and behaviour management effectively. |
| 3. Inclusive Learning Environment | EAS — Effective Use of Additional Staff | Learning support and technicians deployed effectively. |
| 4. Modelling and Professional Language | PC — Professional Communication | Clear, structured, precise explanations; rephrased when needed. |
| 4. Modelling and Professional Language | LM — Live Modelling and Guided Practice | Staff show HOW (talk-alouds); technical concepts demonstrated accurately. |
| 4. Modelling and Professional Language | SSL — Subject Specific Language (CBL) | Technical language taught and reinforced; industry-ready vocabulary. |
| 4. Modelling and Professional Language | ISV — Industry & Sector Vocabulary (WBL) | Learning linked to real-world or workplace scenarios. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | AL — Ambitious Learning | High expectations; challenge; success clearly defined as motivation. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | AE — Active Engagement | Learners actively do, think, apply; know more, can do more, remember more. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | SS — Scaffolding & Support | Support gradually removed; learners succeed and progress independently. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | CL — Collaborative Learning | Learners develop knowledge socially; interact positively with peers. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | LI2 — Learner Independence | Curriculum structures build confident, autonomous, self-regulating learners. |
| 5. Engagement, Collaboration and Independence | AT — Assistive Technology | AT positively promoted; aligned to learning intentions and individual needs. |
| 6. Assessment, Feedback and Progress | CU — Checks for Understanding | Range of techniques; adapted in real time and future sessions. |
| 6. Assessment, Feedback and Progress | EQ — Effective Questioning | Deep thinking; reasoning; opportunities to say and do it better. |
| 6. Assessment, Feedback and Progress | EF — Effective Feedback | Timely, aligned to goals; focused on how learners progress and improve. |
| 6. Assessment, Feedback and Progress | EA — Effective Assessment | Variety of strategies; learners make rapid progress; awarding body met. |
| 6. Assessment, Feedback and Progress | AP — Adaptive Practice | Misconceptions addressed quickly; reasonable adjustments in place. |
| 7. Personal Development and Wellbeing | RTL — Ready to Learn | R.E.A.D.Y expectations; IAG, tutorials, target setting; regular attendance. |
| 7. Personal Development and Wellbeing | RTW — Ready to Work | Employability skills; CEIAG, WEX, IP, WRA, competitive opportunities. |
| 7. Personal Development and Wellbeing | RFL — Ready for Life | Tutorials: EDI, wellbeing, relationships, SG&P, current affairs, FBV. |
| 7. Personal Development and Wellbeing | FS — Future Skills | SMART targets; Future Ready framework; Digital, Academic, Professional, Mindset. |

Hyper focus areas for 2025-26 (college-wide priority — these three must be surfaced prominently in DevObs and LW modules):

- ARD — Accessible by Design (maps to CAT2: Accessible Resources Digital)

- LED — Digital Learning Environment (maps to CAT3: Learning Environment Digital nav)

- AT  — Assistive Technology (maps to CAT5: Assistive Technology)

AFI severity language (from LRA file — use exactly these labels):

- Strength — Genuine strengths, no concerns, would recommend as best practice

- Areas to Strengthen — Tweaks for excellence

- Areas for Immediate Improvement — Rapid change needed; training and support required

**Document 4 — Repository ****&**** File Layout**

**4.1  Repository: gwc25/dpc-hub**

Deployed on GitHub Pages. All files below exist in this repo. No file outside this list should be created without updating this document first.

| **index.html** | Password entry page. Minimal. Validates password (hashed, stored in config.js). On success, redirects to hub.html. |
| --- | --- |
| **hub.html** | Main Hub shell. Loads navigation, tab containers. Reads manifest, loads data files via File System Access API. Single page application. |
