**Document 5 — Build Conventions**

**5.1  Import rules (one-way dependency)**

This rule prevents circular dependencies and keeps the build coherent across sessions:

- schema.js imports nothing. It exports constants only.

- data.js imports from schema.js only. It exports data operations only.

- heuristic.js imports from schema.js only. It exports heuristic functions only.

- Module JS files (devobs.js, afi.js etc) import from data.js, schema.js, and heuristic.js. They do not import from each other.

- app.js imports from all module files. It is the only file that does.

- No module file imports from app.js. The dependency flows one way: app → modules → data/schema/heuristic.

**5.2  Naming conventions**

| **Files** | kebab-case. e.g. devobs.js, learning-walk.js, hub-lite.html |
| --- | --- |
| **JS variables** | camelCase. e.g. areaCode, staffId, lraThemeId |
| **JS constants** | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE. e.g. LRA_TAXONOMY, HYPER_FOCUS, AFI_SEVERITY |
| **CSS custom properties** | --color-navy, --color-teal, --spacing-md. Prefix with category. |
| **JSON keys** | camelCase. Match schema exactly. No exceptions. |
| **IDs in JSON** | Always UUID v4. Never sequential integers. |
| **Dates** | Always ISO 8601. e.g. 2026-07-03. Timestamps: 2026-07-03T09:30:00Z |
| **Enums** | kebab-case strings. e.g. "open", "in-progress", "accessible-by-design" |

**5.3  Accessibility baseline (gate on every UI phase)**

Every UI component must pass these checks before the phase is marked done:

- Colour contrast: minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (WCAG 2.2 AA). Use WebAIM Contrast Checker — pixel-sample backgrounds, do not estimate from CSS tokens alone.

- Keyboard navigation: all interactive elements reachable and operable by keyboard. Focus visible at all times. Tab order logical.

- ARIA: landmark regions on every page (main, nav, aside). Form inputs have associated labels. Modals trap focus. Dynamic content updates announced via aria-live.

- Images and icons: all meaningful images have alt text. Decorative images have alt="".

- Heading hierarchy: one h1 per page. Headings do not skip levels.

- Touch targets (mobile): minimum 44×44px on Hub Lite. No hover-only interactions.

**5.4  Error handling**

- All data.js operations wrapped in try/catch. Errors logged to console with context. User shown a friendly message — never a raw error string.

- File System Access API failures fall back to localStorage gracefully. User notified with clear instruction.

- Supabase failures in Hub Lite show a "Saved locally — will sync later" message. Local backup always attempted first.

- API calls (Anthropic, GitHub) timeout after 15 seconds. User shown a retry option. No silent failures.

- Schema validation on every data load: if a JSON file is missing required fields, log the discrepancy and load with safe defaults rather than crashing.

**5.5  Code style**

- Vanilla JavaScript only in dpc-hub. No frameworks, no build tools, no npm dependencies at runtime.

- ES6+ syntax. Arrow functions, const/let, template literals, destructuring, async/await.

- No inline styles. All styling via CSS custom properties in design.css.

- No inline event handlers in HTML. All events bound in JS via addEventListener.

- Comments on every function: what it does, what it takes, what it returns.

- Version header in every file: // DPC Hub · filename.js · v1.0 · July 2026

**Document 6 — Build Schedule ****&**** Phase Instructions**

Seven phases. Each phase has a precondition (prior phase done-criteria passed), a scope, a file list, build steps, done-criteria including accessibility gate, and a handoff note. No phase starts before its precondition is confirmed.

*EXECUTOR INSTRUCTION: At the start of each phase, re-read Documents 1–5 and this phase**'**s instruction. Do not carry assumptions from a previous session. If the precondition is not met, stop and flag it.*

**PHASE 1 — Foundation: Shell, Data Layer, Schema**

**Precondition**

None. This is the first phase.

**Scope — build**

- index.html — password entry shell

- hub.html — main app shell with navigation skeleton

- css/design.css — full CSS custom property system, WCAG 2.2 AA colour tokens, base layout

- js/config.js — configuration constants

- js/schema.js — LRA_TAXONOMY, AFI_SEVERITY, HYPER_FOCUS, AREA_CODES, all constants from Document 3

- js/data.js — File System Access API logic, manifest loading, auto-save scheduler, localStorage snapshot

- js/app.js — tab routing skeleton, module initialisation stubs

- data/areas-seed.json — 35 areas with codes, names, campus

**Scope — do NOT build in this phase**

- No module JS files beyond app.js stubs

- No Supabase integration

- No content in any tab beyond navigation rendering

**Done-criteria**

- index.html loads, password entry works, redirects to hub.html

- hub.html loads with navigation tabs visible

- File System Access API prompt appears on first load

- Manifest loading function reads dpc-manifest.json correctly from granted folder

- Auto-save fires every 60 seconds (verify via console log)

- localStorage snapshot written on tab close

- WCAG gate: contrast checker passes on all navigation elements and background colours

- No console errors on load

*Handoff: update schema.js version header to v1.0. Confirm LRA_TAXONOMY has all 30 themes from Document 3 Section 3.10.*

**PHASE 2 — Homepage, Calendar, Tasks (Jobs Board)**

**Precondition**

Phase 1 done-criteria confirmed.

**Scope — build**

- js/homepage.js — Jobs Board (post-its), upcoming deadlines (next 14 days), upcoming meetings (next 7 days)

- js/calendar.js — Week/Month/Year views, add/edit/detail for entries, micro-tasks, project linking

- data-calendar.json — initialised with empty structure

**Post-it design spec**

Each task/job appears as a card (post-it style) on the homepage. Card shows: title, due date, linked area or person (if any), status indicator (colour: upcoming=blue, in-progress=amber, overdue=red, complete=green). Click opens full detail modal. Add new post-it via prominent + button. Cards sorted by due date ascending.

**Done-criteria**

- Homepage renders Jobs Board with seed test entries

- Post-it cards show correct fields and status colours

- Click on post-it opens detail modal with full fields editable

- New post-it can be created from homepage and from Tasks section

- Calendar renders in all three views (week/month/year)

- Entry can be added, edited, and deleted

- Upcoming deadlines and meetings sections on homepage populate from calendar data

- WCAG gate: focus visible on all interactive elements, colour contrast passes, keyboard navigable

**PHASE 3 — Areas, RAG Matrix, Quick Capture**

**Precondition**

Phase 2 done-criteria confirmed.

**Scope — build**

- js/areas.js — 35-area overview grid, area detail view, activity log display

- js/rag.js — 8-dimension RAG scoring, snapshot history, rationale entry, trajectory display

- js/quickcapture.js — floating Quick Capture button, activity type selection, LRA theme tagging, saves to area activityLog

- data-areas.json — initialised from areas-seed.json with empty scores

**Done-criteria**

- Areas overview shows all 35 areas with current RAG summary

- Area detail view shows all 8 RAG dimensions with scores, rationale, and last-updated date

- RAG score can be updated; previous scores retained in snapshot history

- Trajectory indicator shows direction of travel where history exists

- Quick Capture opens from floating button, logs an activity to correct area, appears in area activity log

- WCAG gate: RAG colour indicators have text labels (not colour alone), contrast passes

**PHASE 4 — DevObs, Learning Walk, AFI Lifecycle**

**Precondition**

Phase 3 done-criteria confirmed. Neil's final Hyper dropdown wording confirmed (LRA file is the working source — verify exact wording before building dropdown labels).

**Scope — build**

- js/devobs.js — full DevObs modal with LRA category/theme selection, heuristic follow-up questions, Hyper theme tagging (three focus areas prominent), observation rows, AFI auto-draft on save

- js/learningwalk.js — Learning Walk quick capture with LRA tagging, option to escalate to DevObs

- js/afi.js — AFI lifecycle: status transitions, evidence chain display, action selection panel (five options), loop open/close

- js/heuristic.js — coaching question decision tree, AFI auto-draft logic, resource tag matching

**Heuristic AFI auto-draft spec**

When a DevObs is saved with one or more LRA themes tagged:

- For each tagged theme: system evaluates the follow-up question answers

- If answers indicate strength → draft AFI with severity: "Strength"

- If answers indicate partial/developing → draft AFI with severity: "Areas to Strengthen"

- If answers indicate absent/immediate need → draft AFI with severity: "Areas for Immediate Improvement"

- Digital opportunity field auto-populated if theme maps to ARD, LED, or AT

- DPC reviews draft AFI and confirms, edits, or deletes before it is saved

**Done-criteria**

- DevObs modal opens, all 30 LRA themes selectable by category

- Hyper three focus areas (ARD, LED, AT) prominently surfaced at top of theme list

- Follow-up heuristic questions appear after theme selection

- On save, AFI draft appears for DPC review

- Confirmed AFI saved to data-afi.json and referenced in area record

- AFI status can be transitioned through lifecycle

- Evidence chain entries can be added to any AFI

- Action selection panel offers all five intervention types

- Learning Walk logs quickly, LRA themes tagged, escalation to DevObs available

- WCAG gate: modals trap focus, ESC closes, ARIA roles correct

**PHASE 5 — Staff Profiles, Templates, Reflections**

**Precondition**

Phase 4 done-criteria confirmed.

**Scope — build**

- js/staff.js — dynamic profile creation, touch history, development priorities (3), ETF stage, reflection timeline

- js/templates.js — Teach Meet plan builder (Six Stages structure), Coaching Question sets (LRA-themed, AI-draft flagged, DPC approval gate, edit/omit capability), Meeting Agenda templates, Observation Framework templates, versioning, instance creation

- js/reflections.js — event-linked reflection forms, immediate + follow-up stages, follow-up prompt scheduling, anonymous aggregation at area level, AFI evidence wiring

- reflection-form.html — standalone shareable form (separate file, publicly accessible)

**Teach Meet builder spec**

Form organised by Six Stages: Learning Intentions, Building Blocks, Starting Points, Activities, Assessment, Lasting Learning. Each stage has a text area for content and a resource links section (label + URL). Activities section supports multiple timed blocks. Template saved with version number. Instance creation form: add date, area, attendees, context notes, linked AFIs. Editable after creation — each edit increments version; old versions retained.

**Coaching question set spec**

Questions organised by LRA theme. Four question types per set: Opening, Exploring, Challenging, Closing. AI-drafted sets are flagged with a banner: "AI-drafted — pending DPC review." DPC can approve, edit individual questions, omit questions, or add new ones. Only approved sets surface in the heuristic engine. Edit history retained.

**Done-criteria**

- Staff profile created automatically when new name entered in DevObs or LW

- Profile shows full touch history in chronological order

- Three development priorities editable on profile

- ETF stage selectable and displayed

- Teach Meet plan builder follows Six Stages structure, resources addable as links

- Saved template appears in Template Library, filterable by LRA theme

- Template can be edited; version history visible

- Instance created from template with attendees and linked AFI

- Reflection form link generated from instance

- Standalone reflection-form.html accessible without Hub open

- Reflection submission linked to correct event and AFI

- Follow-up reflection prompted at correct interval

- Area overview shows anonymous aggregate reflection themes

- WCAG gate: reflection form fully accessible, form labels correct, no colour-only feedback

**PHASE 6 — Health Checks, Digital Leads, Current Focus, Dashboards, Reports**

**Precondition**

Phase 5 done-criteria confirmed.

**Scope — build**

