**PHASE 7 — CPD Library, Hub Lite, Supabase Sync, AI Support**

**Precondition**

Phase 6 done-criteria confirmed.

**Scope — build**

- gwc25/dpc-cpd-library repo: index.html, css/library.css, js/library.js, js/library-heuristic.js, data/resources.json, data/walkthru-cards.json, data/linkedin-pathways.json, admin/add-card.html, booking.html

- hub-lite.html — mobile surface, Supabase-backed, non-confidential only

- css/hub-lite.css — mobile-first styles

- js/supabase-sync.js — reads pending Hub Lite captures, presents for DPC review, commits to Tier 2

- js/ai-support.js — Strengths synthesis, AFI risk surfacing, action plan generation, report narrative

**CPD Library heuristic search spec**

Trigger word mapping drives search results. User types naturally. System tokenises input and matches against a lookup table:

- questioning / cold call / no hands → EQ (Effective Questioning), CAT6, questioning practice family

- feedback / not acting on / marking → EF (Effective Feedback), CAT6, feedback practice family

- not sticking / remember / retention / recall → LL (Lasting Learning), CAT1, retrieval practice family

- accessible / alt text / contrast / screen reader / AT → ARD or AT, CAT2/CAT5

- Teams / channel / navigation / files → LED, CAT3

- modelling / show / demonstrate / worked example → LM, CAT4

- independent / autonomy / self-regulate → LI2, CAT5

- (expandable — full trigger word table in data/trigger-words.json in dpc-cpd-library repo)

**Done-criteria**

- CPD Library loads publicly without login

- Cards filterable by Six Stage, LRA category, resource type

- Heuristic search returns relevant cards from trigger words

- Admin form adds a new card to resources.json via GitHub API

- Hub Lite loads on mobile, shows Jobs Board surface (title/date/who only)

- Hub Lite Quick Capture submits to Supabase without error

- Hub desktop reads pending Supabase captures and presents for DPC review

- Reviewed captures committed to correct Tier 2 data files

- AI Support synthesises strengths from across area records and staff profiles

- WCAG gate: CPD Library and Hub Lite both pass mobile accessibility checks (touch targets 44px+, contrast, focus)

**Document 7 — Testing Protocol**

Each phase has three test types: Seam Tests (does this connect to what came before?), Feature Tests (does the feature work as specified?), and Accessibility Gate (WCAG 2.2 AA). A phase is not done until all three pass.

**What to ignore (known non-issues)**

- Console warnings from browser extensions — not caused by Hub code.

- File System Access API permission prompts — expected behaviour, not an error.

- Minor layout differences between Chrome and Edge — test in Edge (primary browser).

- Supabase "realtime" connection warnings — Hub Lite uses standard fetch, not realtime subscriptions.

- GitHub API rate limit warnings during development — won't affect production usage.

**What signals a genuine problem**

- Any console error that references a Hub JS file — stop and fix before continuing.

- Data not persisting between sessions — File System Access API not writing correctly.

- JSON schema validation failure on load — data file doesn't match Document 3 schema.

- Any WCAG contrast failure — do not proceed to next phase.

- Focus lost after modal closes — ARIA focus management broken.

- AFI ID referenced in area record not found in data-afi.json — referential integrity broken.

**Checks deferred to first real-run (cannot be verified in development)**

- File System Access API weekly permission reset — only testable after 7 days.

- OneDrive sync latency — depends on college network and OneDrive client.

- Supabase from real mobile device on college WiFi — test on physical device, not browser mobile emulation.

- Anthropic API response time under college network conditions.

**Document 8 — Resource Library Specification**

**8.1  WalkThru Card structure  (walkthru-cards.json)**

| **cardId** | String. UUID. |
| --- | --- |
| **practiceFamily** | String. e.g. "Questioning", "Feedback", "Retrieval Practice", "Modelling", "Explanation", "Collaborative Learning", "Metacognition", "Vocabulary", "Classroom Climate", "Inclusion & SEND", "Curriculum Planning", "Assessment Design", "Independent Practice", "Formative Assessment", "Behaviour & Routines" |
| **title** | String. Practice name (our own words — not Sherrington verbatim). |
| **lraCategoryIds** | Array of strings. LRA categories this maps to. |
| **lraThemeIds** | Array of strings. LRA themes this most directly addresses. |
| **sixStages** | Array of strings. Which Six Stages this practice addresses. |
| **pyramidLevel** | enum: foundations │ inclusion │ innovation │ all. |
| **description** | String. Brief description in our own words. NOT Sherrington text verbatim. |
| **steps** | Array of strings. 3-5 steps. Summarised, not reproduced verbatim. |
| **whatGoodLooksLike** | String. |
| **watchpoint** | String. What superficial use looks like. |
| **digitalConnection** | String or null. Where digital genuinely elevates this practice. Not mandatory. |
| **coachingQuestion** | String. One key coaching question for when this is an AFI. |
| **sourceRef** | String. e.g. "WalkThrus Vol.1 — Tom Sherrington". Not reproduced content. |
| **sourceUrl** | String or null. Free/preview URL if available. Null if behind paywall. |
| **isPublic** | Boolean. True for all library cards. |
| **tags** | Array of strings. Additional search tags. |

**8.2  The 15 practice families — build priority**

Phase 7 initial population: all 15 families seeded with at least 3 cards each. DPC adds further cards via admin form over time.

| **Priority** | **Practice Family** | **Primary LRA Themes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 — High frequency | Questioning | EQ, CU |
| 1 — High frequency | Formative Assessment | CU, EA, AP |
| 1 — High frequency | Feedback | EF, AP |
| 1 — High frequency | Modelling | LM, PC |
| 1 — High frequency | Retrieval Practice | LL, AE |
| 2 — Regular | Explanation | PC, BB |
| 2 — Regular | Collaborative Learning | CL, AE |
| 2 — Regular | Independent Practice | LI2, SS |
| 2 — Regular | Metacognition | SS, LI2, LL |
| 2 — Regular | Inclusion & SEND | AT, ARD, PL |
| 3 — Build over time | Vocabulary & Literacy | SSL, LL2 |
| 3 — Build over time | Curriculum Planning | LI, BB, SP |
| 3 — Build over time | Assessment Design | EA, EF |
| 3 — Build over time | Classroom Climate | PR, RL, BR |
| 3 — Build over time | Behaviour & Routines | BR, RL |

**8.3  LinkedIn Pathway spec**

| **pathwayId** | String. UUID. |
| --- | --- |
| **title** | String. e.g. "Making thinking visible in assessment" |
| **lraThemeIds** | Array of strings. AFI clusters this pathway addresses. |
| **pyramidLevel** | enum: foundations │ inclusion │ innovation. |
| **rationale** | String. When to assign this pathway — e.g. "Assign when AFI identifies gap in real-time assessment practice at ETF Stage 1 or 2." |
| **courseCount** | Number. 2-4 courses. |
| **totalDurationMins** | Number. Approximate. |
| **courses** | Array of { title, url, durationMins, publishedYear }. Only courses from 2022 onwards. |
| **pathwayUrl** | String. LinkedIn Learning shared pathway URL. Added by DPC after creating pathway. |
| **createdBy** | String. "Graeme Wright" |
| **createdAt** | ISO date. |

